  "adaptations": [
    "Place owner cache/Data preparation after allocation of the actual user scratch page.",
    "Place App cryptex helper before its caller and invoke it from macOS Data preparation.",
    "Bind owner boot manifest to this candidate OS UUID, never the iPadOS reference UUID.",
    "Preserve pinned filesystem/owner semantics with ordinary ARM64 callback bridges; no Darwin26 syscall/KPI changes.",
    "Keep paired CodeSignature entitlement constants alongside the CoreEntitlements public API.",
    "Enable actual bindfs sources in the macOS machine configuration for cryptex views.",
    "Publish /System/Volumes/VM as a firmlink to writable owner Data /private/var/vm after Data mount and firmlinks; preserve mount task execution.",
    "Require successful VM firmlink and addon installation before the opt-in APFS boot shim union; propagate errors to checked Data startup.",
    "Port explicit disable-watchdogd=1 launchd bring-up policy after checked Data/shim setup; exclusively create root:wheel 0644 policy and migration marker, verify metadata/readback, refuse existing strategies and propagate errors before launchd.",
    "Explicit disable-watchdogd=1 rejects PID1 direct watchdogd execution and the real xpcproxy argv[1]=com.apple.watchdogd route before child creation; all other proxy jobs and crash/panic policies stay intact.",
    "Explicit nabu-boot-proc=1 records selected final Mach-O activations and committed exit status/reason with bounded argv, ancestry and independent recurring rate limits; no mount, exec, exit or crash policy changes. Ignore retired exec shadow procs before looking up or consuming the live uniqueid trace record.",
    "Explicit nabu-boot-proc=1 records selected abort reason input and saved user registers, with at most six copyin-only frame candidates and independent recurring limits; leaves original abort result and signal policy intact."
  ]
